  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Chronic Crisis - Papua New Guinea Country Operational Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Country Operational Plan MAAPG003</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023: 7500
2024: 100.000</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PNG is exposed to a number of natural, health and human-induced disasters ranging from floods, volcanic eruptions, earthquakes, cyclones, measles, polio, and ethnic and tribal fighting. COVID-19 has further worsened poverty and inequality, and pressure from surging inflation may breed more discontent.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic priorities: 
- building and strengthening climate resilient communities through climate change mitigation, youth education on climate change and partnership and climate adaptation.
-Resilient communities will be developed through effective disaster risk reduction and management including Integrated Vulnerability and Capacity Assessment (IVCA), preparedness and early action, logistic and warehouse management and Emergency Appeal (EA)/DREF response.
-An effective public health programme will be facilitated through advocacy, a health and WASH strategy, community-based health and first aid (CBHFA), epidemic control for volunteer17 (ECV), risk communication and community engagement (RCCE), FA, Epidemic and Pandemic control.
-knowledge and capacity on migration will be improved through AP Regional Migration Network and Humanitarian Service Point (HSPs).</narrative>
  </description>
